      "content": "There is a profound dignity in leaving before the decay becomes too ugly to bear, as it honors your own life by refusing to let it become a monument to suffering. Staying and enduring the decay is not a virtue; it is merely a slow, painful extension of the very thing you are trying to escape. The only true peace comes from making the choice to walk away while there is still a shred of control left in your hands.",
